{
  "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
  "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 02-1343, Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association v. the South Coast Air Quality Management District."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 1967, Congress enacted section 209(a) of the Clean Air Act, which is reproduced in the petitioners' brief at page 1."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, Justice O'Connor, it is a facial challenge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, claiming total preemption."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think the answer to the question at the end of the day, Justice Kennedy, would be that you would require a clearer statement from Congress than what you have in section 209(a) to interfere with the kind of purchasing decisions that localities are -- are making in contrast to this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the purpose of these fleet rules is not simply to restrict the purchases by governmental entities. It is quite clear that the purpose of these fleet rules is to regulate the purchasing choices that are made with respect to a much broader scope of purchasing entities, including private entities, and it is that portion of the regulation, frankly, that we are challenging and challenging on its face."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it's not limited to fleets at all. Under the respondents' theory of this case, the field that has been preempted here really is limited to the manufacturers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Engine Manufacturers Association and Western States Petroleum Association",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I take it what you're challenging is rule 1194 insofar as it applies to private operators."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Because they were enacted at\ndifferent times, I think, the two sections."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The South Coast rules prohibit the purchase of\ncertain motor vehicles and require the purchase of others\nbased on explicit emission standards."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: No, no. I'm not talking about\nwhether their doing of it is unconstitutional. Whether\nthe State's -- whether the State's prescribing that they\ndo it violates the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Waxman (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it\nplease the Court:\nThank you, General Olson.\nThe question in this case is whether section\n209(a) of the Clean Air Act, which is reproduced at page\n36a of our brief, preempts very modest fleet purchase\nrules which apply only to vehicles that are already\ncommercially available, that is, that cannot have an\neffect on manufacture -- cannot require manufacturers to"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "apply for an exemption which the petitioner says is very difficult to get."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's on page 8, footnote 7 of their reply brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State that enacted a provision that authorized these rules has filed a brief in this case saying it applies only when it's commercially available."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, by any theory. Is that preempted or not in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the manufacturers cared about was that they not have to make what is -- was subsequently called a third car."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me start with Justice O'Connor's hypothetical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Kennedy is absolutely right. It has rendered the scope of preemption. There is no field of preemption. There is not even a divot of dirt of preemption that is created under that interpretation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Oh, I think -- no, no, no. With -- with respect, this -- this statute shut down cold, Justice Kennedy, precisely what was going on in 1967."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The one provision that seems to have gotten lost in the -- in all of this, which I think is terribly important, is section 177 which states that State -- and this is at the -- the respondents' brief's appendix at 4a -- 4a. The States are not authorized to prohibit or limit directly or indirectly the manufacture or sale of a new motor vehicle or motor vehicle engine that is certified in California."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carter G. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1343",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "62141f9806f3c438dd3512276e9c4529a4090e72a4bdd1c003ca53678a6089b1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-62141f9806f3-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Oh, absolutely that's just wrong. There is no -- there is no way -- I have seen nothing to justify departing from what the Government's brief says."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
